# Last Updated Comment

## Rule: Keep Top-of-File Comment in Sync

When you **edit any view file** under `views/` (ejs templates), update the **"Last updated"** comment near the top of that file so it reflects the change.

## Where It Appears

- Most view files have an HTML comment on **line 2** (or near the top), e.g.:
  - `<!--  Last Updated: 16 Feb 2026  -->`
  - `<!--  Last updated: 02 Aug 2022  -->`

## What to Do

1. **If you change the page** (content, structure, meta, fixes): set the comment to **today’s date** in this format:
   - `<!--  Last Updated: DD MMM YYYY  -->`
   - Example: `<!--  Last Updated: 24 Feb 2026  -->`
2. Use the **actual date of the edit** (day, three-letter month, four-digit year).
3. If the file has **both** a top-of-file comment and an on-page "Last Updated" (e.g. in legal pages), update **both** so they match.

## Optional

- If you only touch a file trivially (e.g. fix a typo in a comment), you may leave the date unchanged; for any functional or content change, update it.
